---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Badge from "../../components/ui/Badge.astro";
import { SITE } from "../../lib/seo";
import "../../styles/prose.css";

const effectiveDate = "August 30, 2026";
const lastUpdated = "August 30, 2026";
const email = SITE.email;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="WhatsApp Business Platform Terms of Service | SpaceDev"
  description="The terms that govern use of SpaceDev's WhatsApp Business Platform integration service, a Meta Tech Provider connection to the WhatsApp Cloud API."
  noindex={true}
  breadcrumbs={false}
>
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden" style="background: var(--sd-gradient-hero);">
    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-[1100px] px-6 md:px-10 pt-36 pb-20 md:pt-40 md:pb-28">
      <Badge tone="purple" class="mb-6">Legal</Badge>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl text-white">WhatsApp Business Platform Terms of Service</h1>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-col gap-1 text-sm text-sd-text-muted">
        <p>Effective date: <time datetime="2026-08-30">{effectiveDate}</time></p>
        <p>Last updated: <time datetime="2026-08-30">{lastUpdated}</time></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-white py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 md:px-10">
      <article class="sd-prose">
        <h2>1. Agreement</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms govern your use of the WhatsApp Business Platform integration service (the "Service")
          provided by SpaceDev S.A. ("SpaceDev", "we", "us"), a company registered in Uruguay with registered
          office at Bulevar España 2253, Piso 9, Montevideo, Uruguay.
        </p>
        <p>
          By using the Service you agree to these Terms. If you are agreeing on behalf of a company, you confirm
          you have authority to bind it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our handling of data is described separately in our
          <a href="/legal/whatsapp-privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>2. What the Service does</h2>
        <p>
          SpaceDev is a Meta Tech Provider. The Service connects a business phone number to the WhatsApp Cloud
          API through Meta's Embedded Signup, including in Coexistence mode, where the WhatsApp Business App on a
          phone and the Cloud API operate in parallel on the same number.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Service provisions and administers that connection. It does not send messages on your behalf, does
          not provide an inbox or conversation interface, and does not route message traffic through our
          infrastructure.
        </p>

        <h2>3. What the Service is not</h2>
        <p>To avoid misunderstanding, the Service does not include:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>an inbox, CRM, shared mailbox or any conversation interface</li>
          <li>a chatbot or flow builder</li>
          <li>storage, forwarding or replay of message content</li>
          <li>sending messages on your behalf</li>
          <li>conversation analytics</li>
          <li>message billing, credit wallets or resale of Meta messaging</li>
          <li>synchronous support (see section 8)</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Your account and eligibility</h2>
        <p>
          You must be at least 18 and legally able to enter into contracts. You are responsible for the accuracy
          of the information you provide, for the security of your API credentials, and for all activity under
          your account.
        </p>
        <p>
          Notify us at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> if you believe your credentials have been
          compromised.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Your responsibilities</h2>
        <p>You agree to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>comply with the Meta Platform Terms, the WhatsApp Business Terms of Service, the WhatsApp Business Messaging Policy and Meta's Developer Policies</li>
          <li>obtain and maintain any consent required to message the people you contact, under the law applicable to you and to them</li>
          <li>operate and secure the webhook endpoint you configure, and the access tokens delivered to you</li>
          <li>ensure that the WhatsApp Business Account and Meta Business Portfolio you connect belong to the business that sends the messages</li>
          <li>not use the Service for unlawful purposes, spam, or content prohibited by Meta</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          You are responsible for your use of the WhatsApp Business Platform. We provision access; we do not
          supervise how you use it.
        </p>

        <h3>Regulated data</h3>
        <p>
          If your messaging involves health, financial or other regulated categories of data, you are
          responsible for determining whether WhatsApp is an appropriate channel under the law applicable to
          you, and for obtaining any consent required. We do not assess this for you.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Relationship with Meta</h2>
        <p>The Service depends on Meta's platform and is subject to it.</p>
        <p>
          <strong>Meta bills you directly for messaging.</strong> Under Meta's Tech Provider model we do not
          receive a credit line and cannot mark up, resell or rebate WhatsApp conversation charges. You supply
          your own payment method to Meta and pay Meta according to its published rates. Our fees, if any, cover
          our software only and are billed separately.
        </p>
        <p>
          Meta may change its platform, terms, pricing, eligibility criteria and feature availability at any
          time. Meta may suspend or restrict accounts, phone numbers, templates or applications. We do not
          control these decisions and are not responsible for them.
        </p>
        <p>
          Coexistence eligibility is determined by Meta, based on factors including account tenure and messaging
          quality. We cannot obtain it for an account Meta considers ineligible.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Platform risk</h2>
        <p>We want this stated plainly rather than buried.</p>
        <p>
          The Service operates through a Meta application that SpaceDev owns. Permissions over connected WhatsApp
          Business Accounts are held by that application. If Meta restricts, suspends or removes that
          application, connected accounts may lose Cloud API access at the same time.
        </p>
        <p>
          This risk is inherent to the Meta Tech Provider model and applies to every provider operating under
          it. It is a reason to keep the exit path in section 12 available, and a reason not to treat any single
          provider, including us, as a permanent dependency.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Support</h2>
        <p>Support is deliberately limited, and priced accordingly.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Documentation is the support channel.</strong> We maintain written documentation covering setup, routing, error codes and troubleshooting.</li>
          <li><strong>We do not provide email or chat support.</strong> Messages sent to us asking for setup assistance will be redirected to documentation.</li>
          <li><strong>Bug reports</strong> are accepted asynchronously through our public issue tracker, with no service level commitment.</li>
          <li><strong>A 30-minute call is available at USD 100.</strong> This is priced to discourage use. If you need one, we consider it a gap in our documentation and will write the missing page.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>No response time is guaranteed for any channel.</p>

        <h2>9. Availability</h2>
        <p>
          The Service is provided on an "as available" basis. We do not commit to uptime, and we may perform
          maintenance without notice.
        </p>
        <p>
          We may modify or discontinue features. If we discontinue the Service entirely, we will give at least
          <strong>90 days' notice</strong> and keep the exit path in section 12 operational throughout that
          period.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Fees</h2>
        <p>
          Where fees apply, they are stated at signup and billed in advance. Fees are non-refundable except
          where required by law.
        </p>
        <p>
          Non-payment may result in suspension of your access to our API and dashboard.
          <strong>Suspension for non-payment will not deactivate webhook routing for connections already
          provisioned</strong>, so that businesses relying on those connections are not cut off because of a
          billing dispute between you and us.
        </p>
        <p>We may change fees with 30 days' notice.</p>

        <h2>11. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          We retain all rights in the Service, our software and our documentation. You retain all rights in your
          data, your endpoints and your WhatsApp Business Account.
        </p>
        <p>
          You may use our documentation for your own integration work, including copying the prompt templates we
          publish.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Termination and exit</h2>
        <p>You may terminate at any time by disconnecting your connections and closing your account.</p>
        <p>
          We may terminate or suspend your access if you breach these Terms, if required by Meta, or if required
          by law.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>On termination, the WhatsApp Business Account, Meta Business Portfolio and phone number remain
          yours.</strong> We remove our application's subscription to your account. We do not delete, transfer or
          retain your WhatsApp Business Account. You may connect it to another provider or to your own Meta
          application.
        </p>
        <p>
          Procedures for doing so are published in our documentation and are available regardless of the reason
          for termination, including non-payment.
        </p>

        <h2>13. Disclaimers</h2>
        <p>
          THE SERVICE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE", WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED,
          INCLUDING MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NON-INFRINGEMENT.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not warrant that the Service will be uninterrupted or error-free, that Meta will approve any
          account, number or template, or that any message will be delivered.
        </p>

        <h2>14. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, SPACEDEV WILL NOT BE LIABLE FOR INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL,
          CONSEQUENTIAL OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR FOR LOST PROFITS, REVENUE, DATA OR BUSINESS OPPORTUNITY.
        </p>
        <p>
          OUR TOTAL AGGREGATE LIABILITY ARISING OUT OF OR RELATING TO THE SERVICE WILL NOT EXCEED THE GREATER OF
          (A) THE FEES YOU PAID US IN THE TWELVE MONTHS PRECEDING THE EVENT GIVING RISE TO THE CLAIM, OR (B) USD
          100.
        </p>
        <p>Nothing in these Terms excludes liability that cannot be excluded under applicable law.</p>

        <h2>15. Indemnity</h2>
        <p>
          You will indemnify and hold harmless SpaceDev against claims, damages and reasonable costs arising from
          your use of the Service, your messaging content, your breach of these Terms, or your breach of Meta's
          terms or applicable law.
        </p>

        <h2>16. Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these Terms. Material changes will be posted on this page with an updated date, and where
          we have your contact details we will notify you. Continued use after a change constitutes acceptance.
        </p>

        <h2>17. Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms are governed by the laws of the Oriental Republic of Uruguay. The courts of Montevideo
          have exclusive jurisdiction, without prejudice to any mandatory consumer protection rights you may have
          where you reside.
        </p>

        <h2>18. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          SpaceDev S.A.<br />
          Bulevar España 2253, Piso 9, Montevideo, Uruguay<br />
          <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
